TEXT 64 256 Left 2 ;The short circuit current at 2ph+E or 1ph+E is about 9kA at secondary side\nThe three phase short circuit current is about 6kA\nThis is because of the small zero sequence impedance at the z-side of the transformer\nwich is smaller as X1 (X0 e.g ~0.1-0.3*X1)
TEXT 64 224 Left 2 ;I1ph=(3*UN/sqrt(3))/(ZM+ZG+Z0)=(UN/sqrt(3))/((1+1+0.2)*Zk)  If R is small to X set (XM+XG+X0)\nI3ph=(UN/sqrt(3))/Zk
TEXT 64 104 Left 4 ;Low X0 (much lower than X1) at Yzn transformer
TEXT 440 96 Left 2 ;If you know X0 of your YY transformer\nyou can change rkessel (default=1e20) \nto a appropriate value so that your X0 is the simulation result\nAt 1e20 (default)  the magnetic kettleflow is not considered\nHINT: You can see that not only the value of X0 but also\nthe shape of the inrush currents is determined by the kettleflow.\nTherefore for accurate simulation it is important to set rkessel\nto a better value as 1e20
